Morning light slants across the kitchen as Amy flips pancakes for Will and Amber, their laughter filling the air. A sudden crash at the front door shatters the silence; a zombie lurches into the living room, its rotting fingers reaching toward her. She grabs Will’s hand and pulls Amber toward the back stairwell, their tiny feet scuffing against hardwood as she pushes them to a closet behind the pantry. Amy drops her basket of eggs, steps back into the kitchen, and squeezes through the cracked window to retrieve her hidden arsenal. In a pantry alcove behind the fridge, she pulls out a pistol and a katana from their hiding spots. She fires the pistol at one zombie that charges from the hallway, then swings the katana down on another that lunges in; more zombies spill into the kitchen, each attack echoing off tile as she cuts them down one by one. After the last of the zombies collapses with a groan, Amy pulls her kids out of the closet and steps back into the living room together, their breaths ragged but safe.
